		"name": "Project Manager API",
		"description": "Postman collection for the Project Manager ASP.NET Core Web API.\n\n## Prerequisites\n1. MySQL is running with a valid connection string in `appsettings.Development.json`\n2. Run database migration: `dotnet ef database update --project DataAccess --startup-project Api`\n3. Start the API: `dotnet run --project Api`\n4. Default base URL: `http://localhost:5030`\n\n## Recommended Demo Order\nRun the **Demo Flow** folder top-to-bottom using Collection Runner.\nEach Create request saves its ID to a collection variable for the next steps.\n\n## Entities\n- **Users** – project owners\n- **Projects** – belong to a User\n- **Tasks** – belong to a Project and Status\n- **Statuses** – task states (e.g. To Do, In Progress, Done)\n\n## Expected Status Codes\n| Operation | Success |\n|-----------|--------|\n| GET (list / by id) | 200 |\n| POST (create) | 201 |\n| PUT (update) | 204 |\n| DELETE | 204 |\n| Not found | 404 |\n| Validation / constraint error | 400 |\n| Unhandled server error | 500 |",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
